      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T17:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest adding a test that embeds a ternary on the left hand side (e.g. `(((x \u003d\u003d 1) ? y : x) \u003d\u003d z) || ...`) or any other expression that generates additional statements.",
      "revId": "addfe89c2be09e5f329c3bda4411499a38a6a986",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddb2854e_9b7897c2",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLWGSLCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 896,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T16:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In WGSL the `\u0026\u0026` and `||` operators are defined as short-circuiting: https://www.w3.org/TR/WGSL/#logical-expr. So this rewrite is only necessary if the right-hand side expression itself needs to be rewritten as multiple statements.\n\nOf course it doesn\u0027t necessarily hurt to always rewrite them to be sure. I suggest elaborating in the comments about the WGSL language behavior and why we need to rewrite all binary \u0026\u0026/|| operators this way.",
      "revId": "addfe89c2be09e5f329c3bda4411499a38a6a986",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0157f138_89b0fcee",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLWGSLCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 896,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T16:45:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rewrite is always necessary if the `this-\u003eassembleExpression(right)` could ever generate extra freestanding statements, since we need those statements wrapped in an if-block. I\u0027m using `HasSideEffects` here as a stand-in for that check, which might not be a 100% accurate mapping. I should probably make a dedicated function for that.",
      "parentUuid": "ddb2854e_9b7897c2",
      "revId": "addfe89c2be09e5f329c3bda4411499a38a6a986",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9148d7a2_798c5197",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLWGSLCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 896,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T17:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense. I would still elaborate in the comments about the reasons for the rewrite, for example `If the operator is \u0026\u0026 or ||, we need to handle short-circuiting properly in case either side of the expression needed to generate extra statements`. Otherwise short-circuiting still works in the simple case.",
      "parentUuid": "0157f138_89b0fcee",
      "revId": "addfe89c2be09e5f329c3bda4411499a38a6a986",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c645e90f_e8b0855b",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLWGSLCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 914,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T16:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this write `leftExpr` into a scratch variable before writing out the if statement, in case the `leftExpr` itself had to turn into multiple statements (e.g. because it contained a ternary)? This code will need to handle that case eventually.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 914,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 914,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "addfe89c2be09e5f329c3bda4411499a38a6a986",
